<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main id="main">

  <%- include('partials/page-hero', {
    heroImage: project.after,
    eyebrow: project.category,
    eyebrowIcon: 'brush',
    heroTitle: project.title,
    heroIntro: project.summary,
    heroPoints: null,
    breadcrumbs: [{ name: 'Projects', href: '/projects' }, { name: project.title, href: '/projects/' + project.slug }]
  }) %>

  <!-- ============ META ============ -->
  <section class="project-meta">
    <div class="container">
      <ul class="project-meta__grid stagger">
        <li class="project-meta__item reveal">
          <span class="project-meta__label"><%- icon('map', 15) %> Location</span>
          <strong><%= project.location %></strong>
        </li>
        <li class="project-meta__item reveal">
          <span class="project-meta__label"><%- icon('sparkle', 15) %> Service</span>
          <strong><a href="/services/<%= project.service %>"><%= project.serviceName %></a></strong>
        </li>
        <li class="project-meta__item reveal">
          <span class="project-meta__label"><%- icon('clock', 15) %> Duration</span>
          <strong><%= project.duration %></strong>
        </li>
        <li class="project-meta__item reveal">
          <span class="project-meta__label"><%- icon('calendar', 15) %> Completed</span>
          <strong><%= fmtDate(project.date) %></strong>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ BEFORE / AFTER ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section__head section__head--center">
        <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="eyebrow__icon"><%- icon('brush', 15) %></span> The result</p>
        <h2 class="section__title reveal">Before &amp; After</h2>
        <p class="section__lede reveal">Drag or hover the divider to compare. Both photographs were taken on site by our crew lead.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="ba-slider reveal" data-ba>
        <img class="ba-slider__after" src="<%= project.after %>" alt="<%= project.title %> after professional cleaning" width="1200" height="760" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
        <div class="ba-slider__before-wrap">
          <img class="ba-slider__before" src="<%= project.before %>" alt="<%= project.title %> before professional cleaning" width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <span class="ba-slider__label ba-slider__label--before">Before</span>
        <span class="ba-slider__label ba-slider__label--after">After</span>
        <button class="ba-slider__handle" type="button" aria-label="Drag to compare before and after">
          <span><%- icon('arrowLeft', 16) %><%- icon('arrowRight', 16) %></span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CASE STUDY ============ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container content-layout">
      <article class="content-main">
        <div class="case-block reveal">
          <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('alert', 20) %> The Challenge</h2>
          <p><%= project.challenge %></p>
        </div>

        <div class="case-block reveal">
          <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('sparkle', 20) %> What We Did</h2>
          <p><%= project.solution %></p>
        </div>

        <div class="case-block reveal">
          <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('medal', 20) %> The Outcome</h2>
          <p><%= project.result %></p>
        </div>

        <% if (project.scope && project.scope.length) { %>
          <div class="case-block reveal">
            <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('clipboard', 20) %> Scope of Work</h2>
            <p>Everything below was carried out on this job and is listed on the invoice we issued. It is the level of detail we put in writing before we start, not a marketing summary written afterwards.</p>
            <ul class="tick-list tick-list--two">
              <% project.scope.forEach(function (s) { %>
                <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 17) %> <%= s %></li>
              <% }); %>
            </ul>
          </div>
        <% } %>

        <% if (project.lessons && project.lessons.length) { %>
          <div class="case-block reveal">
            <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('bulb', 20) %> What This Means For Your Property</h2>
            <p>The useful part of a job like this is what it teaches about the property type. If you own something similar in Kansas City, these are the things worth knowing before you book anyone:</p>
            <ul class="insight-list">
              <% project.lessons.forEach(function (l) { %>
                <li><%- icon('arrowRight', 17) %> <span><%= l %></span></li>
              <% }); %>
            </ul>
          </div>
        <% } %>

        <div class="case-block reveal">
          <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('list', 20) %> Project At a Glance</h2>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="data-table">
              <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Location</th><td><%= project.location %></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Service delivered</th><td><%= project.serviceName %></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Category</th><td><%= project.category %></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Duration</th><td><%= project.duration %></td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Completed</th><td><%= fmtDate(project.date) %></td></tr>
                <% project.stats.forEach(function (st) { %>
                  <tr><th scope="row"><%= st.label %></th><td><%= st.value %></td></tr>
                <% }); %>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <% if (project.faqs && project.faqs.length) { %>
          <div class="case-block reveal">
            <h2 class="content-block__title"><%- icon('helpCircle', 20) %> Questions This Job Usually Raises</h2>
            <div class="faq-list faq--inline">
              <% project.faqs.forEach(function (f, i) { %>
                <details class="faq"<%= i === 0 ? ' open' : '' %>>
                  <summary class="faq__q">
                    <span><%= f.q %></span>
                    <span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- icon('plus', 18) %></span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="faq__a">
                    <div class="faq__a-inner"><p><%= f.a %></p></div>
                  </div>
                </details>
              <% }); %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% } %>

        <div class="case-quote reveal">
          <span class="case-quote__icon" aria-hidden="true"><%- icon('quote', 30) %></span>
          <p class="case-quote__text">“<%= project.quote.text %>”</p>
          <p class="case-quote__author"><strong><%= project.quote.author %></strong><span><%= project.quote.role %> · <%= project.location %></span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="inline-cta reveal">
          <div class="inline-cta__copy">
            <h3>Have a property like this?</h3>
            <p>Send photographs and we will quote it flat, in writing, with realistic timing — within one business day.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="inline-cta__actions">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact">Get My Free Quote <%- icon('arrowRight', 17) %></a>
            <a class="btn btn--ghost-light" href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%- icon('phone', 17) %> <%= site.phone %></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="content-side">
        <div class="side-card side-card--cta reveal">
          <h3 class="side-card__title">Get This Service</h3>
          <p class="side-card__text"><%= project.serviceName %> across the Kansas City metro, quoted flat before we start.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--block" href="/services/<%= project.service %>">View Service Details</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--block" href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%- icon('phone', 17) %> <%= site.phone %></a>
        </div>

        <div class="side-card reveal">
          <h3 class="side-card__title">More Projects</h3>
          <ul class="side-nav">
            <% projects.filter(function (x) { return x.slug !== project.slug; }).slice(0, 4).forEach(function (x) { %>
              <li>
                <a href="/projects/<%= x.slug %>">
                  <span class="side-nav__icon"><%- icon('brush', 19) %></span>
                  <span class="side-nav__copy">
                    <strong><%= x.title %></strong>
                    <span><%= x.location %></span>
                  </span>
                  <%- icon('chevronRight', 16) %>
                </a>
              </li>
            <% }); %>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn--text btn--block" href="/projects">All projects <%- icon('arrowRight', 16) %></a>
        </div>

        <div class="side-card side-card--trust reveal">
          <h3 class="side-card__title">Every Job Includes</h3>
          <ul class="side-trust">
            <% site.trustBadges.forEach(function (b) { %>
              <li>
                <span class="side-trust__icon"><%- icon(b.icon, 19) %></span>
                <span><strong><%= b.label %></strong><span><%= b.sub %></span></span>
              </li>
            <% }); %>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HOW WE APPROACH THIS WORK ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 class="section__title">How We Approach <%= project.category %> Work</h2>
        <p>
          Every project we take on follows the same structure, whatever the property type. The scope is
          agreed in writing before anyone arrives, the crew is briefed on that scope the morning of the job,
          and the lead walks the property against the same checklist at the end. Nothing about this project
          was improvised, and nothing about yours would be either.
        </p>
        <p>
          The part clients rarely see is the preparation. Before a job like this we confirm access and
          parking, check whether a lift or key collection is needed, verify which surfaces in the property
          need gentler chemistry, and test any unfamiliar product on an inconspicuous area rather than
          applying it to the whole room. Those checks take twenty minutes and prevent the kind of damage
          that takes a fortnight to resolve.
        </p>

        <h3>What We Bring</h3>
        <p>
          Crews arrive with commercial-grade equipment rather than a domestic kit scaled up: HEPA
          triple-filtration vacuums that capture fine dust instead of redepositing it, steamers for grout and
          hard surfaces, extension poles for height without a ladder, colour-coded microfiber separated by
          zone so a restroom cloth never reaches a kitchen, and plant-derived chemistry as the default with
          fragrance-free options available at no extra cost.
        </p>

        <h3>What We Ask of You</h3>
        <p>
          Very little, and we would rather tell you upfront than surprise you. Confirm access arrangements
          and any alarm or lockbox instructions. Tell us about anything delicate, valuable or sentimental
          before the crew arrives rather than during. Let us know if pets will be present and whether they
          should be kept to one area. And if you have a deadline — an inspection, a handover, guests — tell
          us at booking, because that shapes how we staff the job.
        </p>

        <h3>Comparable Work Across the Metro</h3>
        <p>
          This project sits among a wider body of <%= project.category.toLowerCase() %> work across Kansas
          City, Johnson County and the Northland. If your property resembles this one — similar size,
          condition or constraints — the case studies in the sidebar are the closest points of comparison,
          and each one lists the same level of detail on scope, duration and outcome. Reading two or three
          will give you a realistic sense of what your own job involves and roughly what it should cost.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would rather skip the reading, send us photographs of the space with a short description
          and we will tell you which service fits, what it costs and how long it takes — in writing, the
          same day, with no obligation to book.
        </p>

        <h3>Common Mistakes on Jobs Like This</h3>
        <p>
          Across hundreds of similar properties we see the same four mistakes repeatedly, and each one is
          avoidable if you know about it in advance. The first is choosing a provider on price alone without
          comparing scope. A quote that excludes the oven interior, the inside of the windows and the trim
          detail is not cheaper — it is a smaller job wearing a lower number.
        </p>
        <p>
          The second is leaving a booking too late against a fixed date. Move-out inspections, handover
          deadlines and guest arrivals are immovable, and a clean that has to be compressed into half the
          time it needs always shows in the finish. Book with a margin.
        </p>
        <p>
          The third is not declaring the difficult parts upfront — heavy grease, pet odour, hard water
          staining, hoarded rooms. None of these are problems, but they change the products, the dwell time
          and the crew size, and discovering them on the day inevitably means either a rushed job or a
          revised price, neither of which is pleasant for anyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fourth is skipping the walkthrough on a large or unusual property. A twenty-minute visit
          prevents almost every miscommunication that follows, and on jobs above a certain size it is the
          single best use of your time before booking.
        </p>

        <h3>After the Clean</h3>
        <p>
          How you maintain a property after a professional reset determines how long the result lasts. On
          hard flooring, dry vacuuming before any damp mopping is what stops grit from scratching the
          finish. On stone and quartz, pH-neutral products only — abrasive creams dull the surface
          permanently. On grout, letting a cleaner dwell rather than scrubbing harder achieves more with
          less damage.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would like a plan that keeps the property at this standard rather than returning to it in
          a year, a recurring visit at a lower per-clean rate is the more economical route. Many of the
          clients in these case studies started with exactly this kind of one-off reset and moved onto a
          maintenance schedule straight afterwards.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/cta', {
    ctaEyebrow: project.category,
    ctaTitle: 'Let’s Add Your Property to This List',
    ctaText: 'Free walkthrough, a written flat-rate quote the same day, and a crew that turns up when we said it would.'
  }) %>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<button class="to-top" id="toTop" type="button" aria-label="Back to top"><%- icon('chevronDown', 22) %></button>
